  "chapter": 0,
  "number": 0,
  "title": "Sage-kama-oire",
  "jp": "下げ鎌（大入れ）",
  "gloss": "",
  "guidance": "The nuki's end is cut with a 鎌 hook on its underside. The mortise is one hook deeper than the nuki, so the nuki is offered up raised, run home and then dropped: the hook falls behind the post's far face and bears on it, so the nuki cannot be pulled back out. A wedge driven in over the nose seats the nuki on the mortise floor and keeps the hook tight. The nuki is housed at its full section with no shoulder — 大入れ — and the mortise runs right through the post, leaving a narrow cheek either side.",
